What is Shell Scripting?

Shell scripting is the process of automating Linux and Unix operating system tasks using a sequence of commands stored inside a script file.

A shell script allows DevOps engineers to automate:

Server provisioning
Health checks
Log rotation
Backup operations
Application deployment
Monitoring
Incident response
Real-Time Example

Imagine 100 Linux servers.

Without Shell Script:

ssh server1
df -h

ssh server2
df -h

ssh server3
df -h

With Shell Script:

for server in $(cat servers.txt)
do
    ssh $server "df -h"
done
Why DevOps Engineers Use Shell Scripts
Task	Manual Time	Script Time
Disk Check	30 min	10 sec
Log Cleanup	1 hr	5 sec
Deployment	20 min	2 min
Backup	45 min	Automated
